========================================================================
COMPUTATIONAL ARCHITECTURE, PACKAGES, AND ENVIRONMENT SPECIFICATIONS
Project: Sleep Deprivation Meta-analysis (Cross-Platform Transcriptomics)
========================================================================

1. CORE SYSTEM & ENVIRONMENT
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Operating System Platform   : Linux / macOS terminal environments
Base Programming Language   : R Version 4.4.1 (2024-06-14)
Bioconductor Environment    : Version 3.20


2. UPSTREAM RNA-SEQ PIPELINE BINARIES
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Quality Control              : FastQC v0.12.1
Sequence Quality Trimming    : Trimmomatic v0.39
Splice-Aware Read Alignment  : STAR v2.7.10a
Reference Genome             : GRCm39 Mouse Genome
Gene Annotation              : GENCODE vM32
Abundance Quantification     : featureCounts (Subread) v2.0.6

RNA-seq alignment and
quantification are performed
using a GRCm39 reference with
GENCODE vM32 gene annotation.


3. INDIVIDUAL PLATFORM DIFFERENTIAL-EXPRESSION ENGINES
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Microarray Array Processing  : affy v1.84.0
Microarray Normalization     : Robust Multi-array Average (RMA)
Microarray Linear Modeling   : limma v3.62.2
RNA-seq Count Modeling       : DESeq2 v1.46.0

Microarray differential
expression is estimated using
limma empirical Bayes moderated
linear modeling.

RNA-seq differential expression
is estimated using the negative-
binomial generalized linear model
implemented in DESeq2.


4. EFFECT-SIZE AND STANDARD-ERROR EXTRACTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Microarray Effect Estimate    : limma log2 fold change
Microarray Standard Error     : Derived from moderated t-statistic

RNA-seq Effect Estimate       : DESeq2 log2 fold change
RNA-seq Standard Error        : Native DESeq2 lfcSE

For microarray data, standard
errors are calculated from the
limma moderated t-statistic:

    SE = |log2FC| / |t-statistic|

For RNA-seq data, the native
DESeq2 lfcSE is retained without
re-estimation.


5. PLATFORM-SPECIFIC META-ANALYSIS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Meta-analysis Framework       : metafor v4.6-0
Meta-analysis Model            : Random-effects model
Estimation Method              : Restricted Maximum Likelihood (REML)
Small-sample Inference         : Knapp–Hartung adjustment (knha)

Heterogeneity Statistics       :
    - I²
    - tau²
    - 95% prediction interval

Multiple Testing Correction    :
    Benjamini-Hochberg False
    Discovery Rate (FDR)

Microarray and RNA-seq datasets
are first synthesized separately
within their respective platforms.

Platform-specific meta-analysis
is performed using study-level
effect estimates and their
corresponding standard errors.


6. CROSS-PLATFORM SYNTHESIS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cross-Platform Framework       : Precision-weighted effect-size synthesis
Weighting Method               : Inverse-variance weighting
Platform Estimates              :
    - Microarray pooled effect
    - RNA-seq pooled effect

Platform-level estimates are
combined using inverse-variance
precision weighting:

    Weight = 1 / SE²

The resulting cross-platform
analysis reports:

    - Combined log2 fold change
    - Combined standard error
    - 95% confidence interval
    - Two-sided p-value
    - Benjamini-Hochberg FDR

Directional concordance between
microarray and RNA-seq estimates
is evaluated before cross-platform
synthesis.

The cross-platform analysis is
a precision-weighted synthesis of
platform-level random-effects
estimates and is not treated as a
replacement for a full multilevel
study-level model.


7. BRAIN-REGION-STRATIFIED ANALYSIS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Regional Analysis Framework     :
    Region-stratified random-effects
    meta-analysis

Regional Meta-analysis Model    : REML
Small-sample Inference          : Knapp–Hartung adjustment

Regional Heterogeneity Measures :
    - I²
    - tau²
    - 95% prediction interval

Cross-platform regional synthesis:
    Precision-weighted synthesis of
    regional platform-level estimates

Brain-region analyses are performed
using region- and contrast-level
experimental metadata where available.

Datasets containing multiple brain
regions, time points, or experimental
contrasts are not assumed to represent
a single independent observation.


8. MICROARRAY PROBE SELECTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Probe Selection Principle        :
    Treatment-independent selection

Gene-level probe selection is based
on mean expression rather than the
magnitude of the observed treatment
effect.

This avoids selecting probes according
to their sleep-deprivation-associated
effect size and thereby reduces
outcome-dependent selection bias in
the downstream meta-analysis.


9. DATA WRANGLING & VISUALIZATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data Manipulation                : dplyr
Data Restructuring               : tidyr
Iterative Workflows              : purrr
Statistical Visualization        : ggplot2
Heatmap Visualization            : pheatmap
Network Visualization             : igraph / ggraph
Meta-analysis                    : metafor


10. PRIMARY SIGNIFICANCE CRITERIA
------------------------------------------------------------------------
False Discovery Rate             : FDR < 0.05
Effect-size threshold             : |log2FC| >= 1

Genes satisfying both criteria
are retained as significant
cross-platform or regional
meta-analysis findings,
as appropriate to the analysis.


11. SOFTWARE REPRODUCIBILITY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
All software versions listed above
should be retained with the analysis
environment when reproducing the
computational workflow.

Reference genome and annotation
versions should remain consistent
between RNA-seq alignment,
quantification, and downstream
gene-level analysis.

